{
  "summary": "A minimalist, monochromatic interactive experience where a central typographic element transforms into dynamic, physics-driven particles upon user interaction. The system uses a prompt-based input to allow real-time content modification while maintaining a strict, clean aesthetic with high-contrast elements and spacious layouts.",
  "style": {
    "description": "Monochromatic and technical. The palette is anchored by a warm off-white background (#f5f3f0) and pure black (#000000) for all text and UI elements. Typography relies exclusively on 'Space Grotesk' in varying weights, emphasizing large, tight-tracked hero text and tiny, widely-tracked metadata. Animation is central, utilizing a particle system with three distinct primitive types (dots, rings, crosses) and physics-based behaviors like friction, easing, and radial dispersion.",
    "prompt": "Create a design system using an off-white background (#f5f3f0) and black text (#000000). Typography: Use 'Space Grotesk'. Hero text should be font-weight 500, font-size 14vw, with letter-spacing -0.05em. UI labels should be font-size 8px to 10px, uppercase, with tracking 0.2em to 0.3em. UI elements: Use 1px borders with 10-20% black opacity. Cursor: Implement a custom 12px black circle cursor with 'mix-blend-mode: difference' that disappears when hovering interactive text elements. Particle System Details: Generate particles from text silhouettes using a 2px grid. Particle types: 92% dots (filled), 4% rings (stroked, 0.5px width), 4% crosses (stroked, 0.5px width). Physics: 200px interaction radius, friction 0.95, ease 0.05-0.1, with a continuous slow drift (velocity +/- 0.5px per frame)."
  },
  "layout_and_structure": {
    "description": "A fixed-frame layout that prioritizes a large central interaction zone, framed by technical metadata and navigation at the screen edges.",
    "prompts": [
      {
        "part": "Header",
        "prompt": "Fixed header at top: 48px (top: 12) from screen edge, 48px padding on sides. Left side: metadata tag in 10px uppercase text, tracking 0.3em. Right side: A vertical stack containing a text input field and a sub-label. Input field: 256px width (w-64), transparent background, border-bottom 1px black (10% opacity), text-align right, font-size 14px. Sub-label: 8px uppercase text, tracking 0.2em, 30% opacity black."
      },
      {
        "part": "Interaction Zone",
        "prompt": "Centered hero area. Large display text (14vw) that remains invisible while particles are active during hover. An invisible trigger overlay (z-index 30) spans the text dimensions to capture mouse events. Particle canvas (z-index 10) covers the full viewport, rendering the text as a collection of primitives."
      },
      {
        "part": "Footer",
        "prompt": "Fixed footer at bottom: 48px (bottom: 12). Center-aligned elements: a horizontal divider (96px width, 1px height, 20% opacity black) followed by a 10px uppercase text label with 0.2em tracking at 30% opacity."
      }
    ]
  },
  "special_ui_components": [
    {
      "component": "Prompt Input Field",
      "description": "A minimalist text input that controls the central generative experience.",
      "prompt": "Style a text input with no background and no border except a thin 1px bottom border at #0000001a (10% opacity). On focus, the border should darken to #00000066 (40% opacity). The text should be right-aligned, uppercase, tracking-wide, and responsive to real-time keystrokes to trigger particle re-generation."
    },
    {
      "component": "Physics-Based Particle Text",
      "description": "Typographic particles that react to cursor proximity.",
      "prompt": "Implement a canvas-based particle system where particles form a text string. On hover: particles within 200px of the mouse should move away from the cursor along a vector calculated from the center, with a force of (200 - distance) / 200 * 15. On mouse leave: particles should snap back to their original 'text shape' coordinates using a random ease value between 0.05 and 0.1 for a fluid, natural motion."
    }
  ],
  "special_notes": "MUST: Ensure font-family 'Space Grotesk' is fully loaded before calculating particle coordinates from the canvas pixel data. MUST: Toggle visibility of the static hero text to 0 opacity instantly upon hover to reveal the underlying particles. MUST NOT: Use colors other than #f5f3f0 and #000000; all depth must be achieved via opacity layers (10%, 20%, 30%, 40%, 70%). MUST: Keep the particle density responsive by adjusting the sampling gap based on string length and screen width."
}

{
  "summary": "A sophisticated dark-mode design system for technical monitoring, featuring a deep navy base (#020617), vibrant cyan accents (#22d3ee), and highly legible typography for complex data visualization. The layout uses a modular card-based structure with subtle glassmorphism and grid-based alignment.",
  "style": {
    "description": "The style is 'Industrial-Cyberpunk Minimalist.' It pairs the approachable 'Plus Jakarta Sans' for UI elements with 'JetBrains Mono' for technical data. The color palette is strictly controlled to maintain high contrast while reducing eye strain. Animations are purposeful, utilizing smooth cubic-bezier transitions for hover states and subtle pulses for live indicators.",
    "prompt": "Create a UI style based on a dark navy theme. \n- **Core Palette**: Background: `#020617`; Card Surfaces: `#0f172a`; Hover/Highlight Surfaces: `#1e293b`; Primary Accent: `#22d3ee` (Cyan); Muted Text: `#94a3b8`; Bright Text: `#f8fafc`; Border Color: `#334155`.\n- **Functional Colors**: Success: `#10b981`; Warning: `#f59e0b`; Error: `#f43f5e`; Neutral/Inactive: `#334155`.\n- **Typography**: Primary font is 'Plus Jakarta Sans'. Use 'JetBrains Mono' for all time-stamps, IDs, and numeric values. Heading sizes: 18px bold for page titles, 14px bold for section headers, 12px for body, and 9-10px for labels/tags with 0.05em tracking.\n- **Visual Effects**: Cards use a 1px solid border (`#334155`). Backgrounds feature a radial-gradient grid pattern (`rgba(51, 65, 85, 0.4) 1px`, 20px spacing). Use `box-shadow: 0 20px 25px -5px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1)` for elevated cards. \n- **Animations**: Hover states transition over 0.2s using `cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)`. Active status indicators use a 2s infinite pulse animation."
  },
  "layout_and_structure": {
    "description": "A vertical-scrolling modular layout optimized for wide screens (1600px max). It transitions from high-level summaries to actionable triage items, a daily timeline view, and finally a dense comparison matrix.",
    "prompts": [
      {
        "part": "Sticky Header",
        "prompt": "Design a sticky header (height: 64px) with background `#0f172a` and a bottom border `#334155`. Left side: Logo slot with a 40px rounded-lg cyan icon container and two-tier text (Title: 18px bold; Subtitle: 10px uppercase tracking-wider). Right side: Live status pill with a pulsing emerald dot, a vertical divider, and a Mono-spaced ID badge. Include a square icon button for refresh actions."
      },
      {
        "part": "Metric Summary Grid",
        "prompt": "A 4-column grid of summary cards. Each card: background `#0f172a`, 16px padding, 12px border-radius. Each card must have a 4px solid left border colored according to the status (Cyan, Rose, Indigo, Emerald). Inside, place a 40px circular icon background (10% opacity of the accent color) and stacked text: Label (10px muted) and Value (14px bold Mono)."
      },
      {
        "part": "Triage & Findings Panel",
        "prompt": "A full-width glass-card with a header row showing item counts in color-coded badges (e.g., '3 Errors' in Rose). Content is an accordion list. Items (finding-rows) use `1e293b` on hover. Each row includes: Severity Icon, Day Tag (9px bold), Time Slot (Mono), Description (Text-muted), and a compact Cyan action button (10px bold, 4px padding-x)."
      },
      {
        "part": "Daily Timeline Ribbon",
        "prompt": "A horizontal scrollable container showing a 24-hour strip. Background is the radial grid pattern. Use a vertical 2px Emerald line to represent 'NOW' with a labeled flag. Time slots are colored blocks (Cyan, Amber, or Slate-600) with thin borders. Y-axis: 4-step time markers (00, 08, 16, 24) in 9px Mono."
      },
      {
        "part": "Comparison Matrix",
        "prompt": "A dense data grid with a sticky left column for labels (e.g., Days of the Week). Each row is 80px high and split into two horizontal tracks: 'Track K' (User) and 'Track C' (Device). Use specific color blocks to indicate activity. Track K uses Cyan/Amber; Track C uses the same or a specific error state (Rose background with 'DISCONNECTED' text). A top header row provides 4-hour interval timestamps (00:00, 04:00, etc.) in 9px Mono."
      }
    ]
  },
  "special_ui_components": [
    {
      "component": "Status Badge Pulse",
      "description": "A live-data indicator used in the header and status cards.",
      "prompt": "A 8px circle with a background color of `#10b981`. Apply an animation named 'pulse' that scales the shadow from `0 0 0 0 rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.7)` to `0 0 0 8px rgba(16, 185, 129, 0)` over a 2s duration, repeating infinitely."
    },
    {
      "component": "Dual-Track Data Row",
      "description": "Visualizing two data sources (User vs Machine) in parallel.",
      "prompt": "A container with height 80px. Split into two 40px sub-rows. Bottom sub-row has a border-top of `#334155/20`. Each track contains absolute-positioned divs representing time segments. These segments use `border-radius: 2px` and specific accent colors. Include a label 'K' and 'C' at the start of each track with 50% opacity."
    }
  ],
  "special_notes": "Must maintain high contrast for accessibility—never use cyan text on a white background. All numeric codes must use JetBrains Mono for vertical alignment consistency. Cards must have a 1px border to distinguish them from the deep navy background. Do not use border-radii larger than 16px to keep the technical, rigid aesthetic."
}

{
  "summary": "A record-label landing page whose hero is a portal: two panels part outward to uncover a full-bleed image while the wordmark grows, its tracking tightens and its two halves travel to opposite edges. The catalogue below is a physical deck of sleeves you throw aside.",
  "style": {
    "description": "Near-black ground with a warm bone ink, one amber accent and one teal, both taken from the photography so the page and the image are the same palette. A wide geometric display face carries every heading; a neutral sans carries all small type at wide tracking.",
    "prompt": "Apply a dark label style. Palette: ground #0A0C0E, secondary ground #101317, ink #EDE7DC, secondary ink #9EA5A8, muted #6C7378, amber #E8913C, teal #2E6B72, hairlines rgba(237,231,220,.13). Typography: 'Syne' 600-800 for the wordmark and headings at letter-spacing -.02em to -.03em; 'Sora' 400-600 at 10.5-16px, with labels uppercase at letter-spacing .12em-.15em. Pull the two accents OUT of the hero photograph so the interface and the image agree. MUST keep both accents to type, a dot or a rule, never a filled area. DO NOT use a gradient banner, a bento grid, a glow, or a drop shadow on anything except the deck cards."
  },
  "layout_and_structure": {
    "description": "Six sections. A tall portal hero with a sticky stage, a full-height statement fold, a two-column releases section carrying a throwable deck, a hairline roster, a dates table, and a close whose wordmark is cropped by the page edge.",
    "prompts": [
      {
        "part": "Navigation",
        "prompt": "Fixed 58px bar on a translucent ground with a 14px backdrop blur and a bottom hairline. Display wordmark at 15px with a trailing period in the amber, uppercase links at 10.5px turning amber on hover, one pill button."
      },
      {
        "part": "Portal hero",
        "prompt": "A tall section, roughly two and a half viewports, containing a sticky full-height stage with overflow hidden and isolation isolate. Layer, back to front: a full-bleed image starting somewhat overscaled; a duotone wash blending the two accents at mix-blend-mode overlay and zero opacity; a radial veil darkening the edges; TWO solid panels each a little over half the width, pinned to the left and right edges so they meet in the middle and the hero begins CLOSED; two small glowing accent dots at the centre; and the wordmark on top, split into two spans. Corner metadata pins to the top and bottom edges."
      },
      {
        "part": "Statement fold",
        "prompt": "A full-height section holding a small uppercase label, a statement at clamp(24px,3.6vw,52px) over about 22ch with one phrase in the amber, an outlined index numeral using -webkit-text-stroke with a transparent fill, and a circular image floating off the right edge at reduced opacity that drifts and rotates on scroll."
      },
      {
        "part": "Releases",
        "prompt": "Two columns: a headline, a lede and two buttons on one side; the deck on the other, square, with a hint line and progress dots beneath it."
      },
      {
        "part": "Roster and dates",
        "prompt": "Hairline-ruled rows carrying a small uppercase accent label, a display-face name and a right-aligned count. Then a table with uppercase headers over a hairline, a display-face first column and neutral metadata columns, collapsing to a two-column grid per row on narrow screens."
      },
      {
        "part": "Close",
        "prompt": "A short headline, a fine-print line, two buttons at the opposite edge, a hairline footer strip, then the wordmark full width, translated down slightly so the page edge crops it."
      }
    ]
  },
  "special_ui_components": [
    {
      "component": "The portal title",
      "description": "The signature move: the wordmark grows while its tracking tightens and its halves separate.",
      "prompt": "Split the wordmark into two spans on one line. As scroll progresses through the hero, scale the whole title UP by a modest amount while SIMULTANEOUSLY tightening its letter-spacing, and translate the first span left and the last span right by roughly half their own width. Growing and tightening at the same time is the entire point: it reads as a title opening rather than a plain zoom, and doing one without the other loses the effect. Pick the exact amounts against your own typeface — a wide geometric face needs less tightening than a condensed one. Drive it all from scroll POSITION so it plays in reverse when the reader scrolls back up."
    },
    {
      "component": "The portal opening",
      "description": "How the hero uncovers its image.",
      "prompt": "Two opaque panels start meeting in the middle so the hero begins closed. On scroll translate them outward past their own width so they clear the frame entirely, uncovering the image behind. At the same time settle the image from a slight overscale down to 1, raise a duotone overlay from zero to a low opacity, and send two accent dots travelling out toward opposite corners of the field. Keep every value bound to scroll position, never to a timer, so the portal closes again as the reader scrolls up."
    },
    {
      "component": "Throwable card deck",
      "description": "The catalogue as a physical stack you flip through.",
      "prompt": "Stack the cards absolutely, offsetting each successive one slightly across, up, down in scale and in rotation so the stack reads as physical. On pointerdown capture the pointer and drop the transition; on pointermove track the drag with a translate plus a rotation proportional to the horizontal distance and a very slight scale up; on release, if the drag passed a threshold of roughly a tenth of the deck width, throw the card out across the deck's own width with a small lift and a roll in the direction of travel, then re-stack with the next card on top. Give the deck tabindex 0 and left/right arrow handlers, and set touch-action: pan-y so vertical scrolling still works on a phone. The deck must be usable without a mouse."
    },
    {
      "component": "Motion models",
      "description": "What is reversible and what is not.",
      "prompt": "Everything in the portal is bound to scroll position and therefore plays both ways. Entry reveals elsewhere fire once and must NOT un-reveal. Scope all reveal rules to a class added only after confirming prefers-reduced-motion is not set, so the reduced-motion and no-JS renders are the finished page. Verify the hero actually travels: something in it should move well over 100px across the first 700px of scroll, measured rather than assumed."
    },
    {
      "component": "Evidence rules",
      "description": "What the page may claim.",
      "prompt": "Only the label's own catalogue and dates. DO NOT invent press quotes, chart positions, streaming counts or award badges. Keep every release code, date and count internally consistent."
    }
  ]
}

